{
  "_readme": [
    "Human classification of every clip in the manifest, made by VIEWING six evenly",
    "spaced frames per clip (see sheets.py; the sheets are in $BENCH_WORK/sheets).",
    "It is NOT derived from any detector output — that would make the bench mark its",
    "own homework.",
    "",
    "class:  full_swing | chip | putt | not_a_shot",
    "  full_swing  a struck shot that leaves the ground and flies. THE TRACER MUST",
    "              WORK ON THESE. This is the denominator of the honest hit rate.",
    "  chip        greenside/bunker/pitch. Real contact, but little or no flight.",
    "              A refusal here is acceptable; an arc is a bonus.",
    "  putt        the tracer MUST refuse. A refusal counts as CORRECT, not a miss.",
    "  not_a_shot  no golf stroke in the clip at all (walking, a trolley, raking, an",
    "              empty green). MUST refuse. Excluded from the hit-rate denominator",
    "              entirely; drawing an arc here is the worst possible outcome.",
    "",
    "conf:   clear | low.  'low' means six frames were not enough to be sure — the",
    "        swing may fall between samples. Reported separately so a number is never",
    "        quoted as if every label were solid."
  ],
